  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-12-15T05:36:11.878Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The recent update has slightly screwed up player animations, especially custom ones. The blending of running animations appears to have been changed such that the upper body no longer moves naturally. This isn't all that noticeable on the default avatars, but many of my avatars look absolutely bizarre when they run now. Also, players comically lean forward when they run now.\n\nAdditionally, the increased time in blending between the idle and running animations has screwed up many of my avatars. I used to use animation overrides to toggle separate meshes that did the idle and running animations, but now because of the increased blend time there's a few seconds where if I start running from a standstill both the running and idle meshes are visible at the same time.\n\nAlso, sitting animations have been screwed up for many custom avatars. I've seen people's spines bend in odd directions when they sit, and apparently their viewpoint gets messed up to, although I have yet to experience this. I've also seen players with overrides for their sitting animations have those completely messed up as well. Now their heads get moved down about a foot so they're completely hunched over.",
